 -  assumes you hava java-25
 -  running 'mvn clean install' in the root project will build both images
 -  you can check that via 'docker images | grep sample'

 -  create local cluster: 'kind create cluster'
 -  load the image into the cluster : 'kind load docker-image front:latest'
                                      'kind load docker-image backend:latest'

 - kubectl apply -f backend/src/main/resources/k8s/
 - kubectl apply -f front/src/main/resources/k8s/

 - find the ID of kind : docker ps ( shown here : 5dc9b97a179f )
 - docker exec -u 0 --privileged -it 5dc9b97a179f bash

 - kubectl get pods -o wide
   ( get the IP of the front )

 - curl 10.244.0.6:8080

 will output DONE, meaning it was loadbalanced to backend
